y further vaccine  development  in this context i'm glad to inform you  that the member states have agreed  to trigger a first tranche of over 180  million extra doses  of adapted vaccines in our third  contract with biotech pfizer  finally a word on the certificate in the  times of pandemic i inform the leaders  that the commission will present a  delegated act  we will ensure a common approach on  boosters and the length of validity of  the certificate  so boosters are recommended at the  latest six months after full vaccination  and the certificate will remain valid  for grace period of three months beyond  this  briefly turning to migration  we reflected on how we can draw lessons  from our answers to the hybrid attack at  the our borders with belarus  and we agreed to work on two strands the  first one is strengthening the  cooperation with countries of origin and  transit to improve the situation on  returns  janice yanza has described the success  that we had with vice president skinners  reaching out to countries of origin  to do this  to draw the lesson from this successful  action  i will set up a european coordination  for external aspects of migration at the  level of vice president skinners and  commissioner johansson  and this proposal was very well received  by the leaders  second  we will make sure that the eu legal  framework is fit for purpose  in particular to address this so-called  instrumentalization of people like it  happened in belarus  the commission is also delivering on  this  because this week we proposed changes to  the schengen border code covering both  the external as well as the internal  borders  and finally of course i reminded leaders  that to make the most out of these  efforts we need to work on a swift  adoption of the pact on migration and  asylum  and this leads me to the last topic that  is ukraine and russia  our concern related to russia's military  buildup on the eastern ukrainian borders  are well known  our position is